WEBVTT

1
00:00:09.767 --> 00:00:14.431
Having changed into her old but still pretty blue dress and pulled back her damp hair into a

2
00:00:14.491 --> 00:00:18.935
tidy bun, Amy was once again the eager hostess ready to greet her guests.

3
00:00:19.836 --> 00:00:23.199
She waited and waited worriedly for any signs of the arrival of the girls.

4
00:00:24.079 --> 00:00:28.623
But an hour or so later, after the rain had stopped and short bursts of sunshine had broken

5
00:00:28.663 --> 00:00:32.249
through the clouds, not a single guest had appeared at the March home.

6
00:00:33.749 --> 00:00:39.371
Amy wrung her hands, her face crumbling in disappointment as she craned her neck for any familiar faces

7
00:00:39.451 --> 00:00:39.971
on the street.

8
00:00:40.931 --> 00:00:47.513
Her family stood a little behind her, aching to console her but letting her retain some dignity.

9
00:00:48.353 --> 00:00:50.514
It was obvious the party was ruined.

10
00:00:50.534 --> 00:00:58.156
"Just wait till I get my hands on those sissy, prissy, no-good brats," Jo mumbled under her breath,

11
00:00:58.528 --> 00:01:03.831
cracking her knuckles as she pondered ways to get revenge on those who had hurt her sister.

12
00:01:03.851 --> 00:01:08.193
"Jo! You're not helping the situation," Mother whispered loudly.

13
00:01:08.213 --> 00:01:14.017
"Well, I don't think we'll be having any guests today," Amy called out with forced cheeriness.

14
00:01:14.037 --> 00:01:18.479
"Maybe they got lost," suggested Beth kindly.

15
00:01:19.299 --> 00:01:23.682
Amy let out an ugly laugh and said, "I doubt it, dear sister.

16
00:01:24.122 --> 00:01:27.244
More likely they all agreed not to come to teach me a lesson."

17
00:01:28.136 --> 00:01:30.678
"It's because they're jealous of you," offered Jo.

18
00:01:30.698 --> 00:01:35.100
"You're beautiful and talented, and you have a family that adores you."

19
00:01:36.581 --> 00:01:41.283
Shaking her head Amy said, "Thanks, Jo, but it's plain to see that the girls want me to

20
00:01:41.343 --> 00:01:44.405
know my place that I don't belong among them.

21
00:01:45.346 --> 00:01:50.429
They let me visit their mansions and castles, as if they're doing me a favor, but they won't

22
00:01:50.529 --> 00:01:52.730
set foot in a humble home like ours."

23
00:01:54.431 --> 00:01:59.253
Father wrapped his arm around Amy and said, "I'm not excusing those girls for how they hurt you

24
00:01:59.293 --> 00:02:06.235
today, dear, but whatever their reasons were, don't lose your self-worth or your pride in who you are."

25
00:02:06.255 --> 00:02:13.877
"Thank you, Father, and all of you, for your help and for bearing with me," Amy smiled sheepishly.

26
00:02:13.897 --> 00:02:16.558
"I know I've been such a bother this week."

27
00:02:16.578 --> 00:02:23.460
"It was our pleasure," Mother replied, giving Jo a stern look before she could say anything.

28
00:02:24.324 --> 00:02:26.665
"Now, what are we going to do with all this food?"

29
00:02:28.306 --> 00:02:32.409
Over at the newlyweds' house, Meg's day was not faring any better than Amy's.

30
00:02:33.349 --> 00:02:36.331
John had invited some of his friends over for dinner that evening.

31
00:02:37.291 --> 00:02:42.114
Although Meg had felt confident when she had agreed to prepare a meal all by herself, she was

32
00:02:42.174 --> 00:02:45.776
wondering now how on earth she had gotten herself into such a pickle.

33
00:02:47.316 --> 00:02:54.381
"Two cups of butter, no, one cup butter and one cup oil, no, that doesn't sound right Oh!

34
00:02:54.461 --> 00:02:55.122
I don't know.

35
00:02:55.342 --> 00:02:56.282
I can't remember!"

36
00:02:56.583 --> 00:02:59.585
Meg cried as she tried to recall the ingredients in apple pie.

37
00:03:00.625 --> 00:03:06.089
Frustrated, Meg decided to make the creamed chicken first but could not find a clean pot to make

38
00:03:06.129 --> 00:03:10.592
the sauce in, because all her dishes were either dirty or being used.

39
00:03:11.873 --> 00:03:17.177
At home, Meg had always relied on Hannah to wash the dishes while she cooked, and another person

40
00:03:17.237 --> 00:03:20.658
to help her prepare the vegetables or hand her the ingredients she needed.

41
00:03:22.059 --> 00:03:26.861
As the mistress of her own home and without a helper (John's modest salary did not allow them

42
00:03:26.901 --> 00:03:31.443
to hire someone at the moment), Meg had to do everything on her own and it was driving

43
00:03:31.483 --> 00:03:31.923
her mad.

44
00:03:31.943 --> 00:03:36.325
"Oh! I should just tell John to cancel tonight's dinner.

45
00:03:36.686 --> 00:03:37.506
I can't do it!"

46
00:03:37.926 --> 00:03:41.808
said Meg, dropping into a chair, where she held her head and began crying.

47
00:03:43.228 --> 00:03:47.611
A light gentle rap on the window, then a louder one, forced Meg to look up with red

48
00:03:47.791 --> 00:03:53.756
eyes. Jo was peering in with a worried expression, mouthing something Meg could not understand.

49
00:03:55.457 --> 00:03:59.300
Wiping her tears, Meg stood up and opened the door to let her sister in.

50
00:03:59.320 --> 00:04:01.401
"What's the matter, Meg?"

51
00:04:01.821 --> 00:04:04.503
Jo demanded, taking hold of her sister's hand.

52
00:04:04.523 --> 00:04:08.326
"I'm so glad to see you, Jo," sniffed Meg.

53
00:04:08.846 --> 00:04:10.868
"How is everything going with Amy's luncheon?"

54
00:04:11.516 --> 00:04:14.938
Snorting loudly, Jo explained what had happened while Meg listened intently.

55
00:04:16.339 --> 00:04:17.519
"Poor Amy!"

56
00:04:17.820 --> 00:04:20.041
Meg said, forgetting her own plight at once.

57
00:04:20.061 --> 00:04:27.405
"Yes, but our Amy is a fighter," said Jo proudly, "and she's already put this incident behind her.

58
00:04:27.785 --> 00:04:28.806
She'll be fine.

59
00:04:29.486 --> 00:04:31.147
Now what is going on here?"

60
00:04:31.167 --> 00:04:34.029
"I'm such a horrible wife!"

61
00:04:34.429 --> 00:04:36.270
Meg began, tears forming again.

62
00:04:36.290 --> 00:04:38.831
"Don't say such things.

63
00:04:39.111 --> 00:04:39.992
That's not true.

64
00:04:40.480 --> 00:04:42.322
Tell me how I can help," said Jo.

65
00:04:43.283 --> 00:04:47.126
Meg explained what she was doing and why things weren't going as smoothly as she'd like.

66
00:04:47.146 --> 00:04:53.352
"I didn't want to ask you or Mother since I knew Amy needed your help, and besides, I

67
00:04:53.432 --> 00:04:55.894
thought I could manage on my own," Meg said.

68
00:04:55.914 --> 00:04:58.216
"Why doesn't John help you?"

69
00:04:58.696 --> 00:05:02.620
asked Jo, still looking for an excuse to dislike the man who had taken Meg away from her.

70
00:05:03.720 --> 00:05:08.523
"I'm afraid I'm to blame since I sent him out early this morning on a few errands because

71
00:05:08.563 --> 00:05:11.725
I didn't want him to get in my way," Meg said, shamefaced.

72
00:05:12.546 --> 00:05:17.769
As Jo sized up the situation, she realized that Meg was in trouble and desperately needed help.

73
00:05:18.649 --> 00:05:20.931
In a flash, Jo had a great idea.

74
00:05:20.951 --> 00:05:23.352
"Meg," she said excitedly.

75
00:05:23.372 --> 00:05:29.056
"Clean up this mess, clean yourself off, put on your lovely dress, and leave the rest to me."

76
00:05:30.136 --> 00:05:31.757
"Jo, are you out of your mind?

77
00:05:32.077 --> 00:05:35.138
The guests will be here in two hours," Meg said impatiently.

78
00:05:35.158 --> 00:05:37.960
"Please, Meg, I have an idea.

79
00:05:38.380 --> 00:05:40.401
Just trust me," Jo begged.

80
00:05:41.181 --> 00:05:42.882
Meg stared at her sister warily.

81
00:05:43.902 --> 00:05:48.564
Something about Jo's voice and manner persuaded Meg to trust her, so she did as Jo asked.

82
00:05:49.545 --> 00:05:54.227
After cleaning up the kitchen and washing the dishes, Meg took a long bath and changed her clothes.

83
00:05:55.227 --> 00:06:00.049
With no sign of Jo, Meg anxiously tidied her small living room and set out the cutlery and

84
00:06:00.089 --> 00:06:03.650
china plates purchased with Aunt March's generous wedding gift.

85
00:06:05.010 --> 00:06:09.512
Then she paced the kitchen floor, her heart racing as her eyes skimmed the bare table.

86
00:06:10.252 --> 00:06:14.653
Meg was beginning to feel sorry for John, who would be coming home to find nothing ready for

87
00:06:14.693 --> 00:06:20.135
his guests, when her ears picked up the sounds of a horse trotting, then stopping in front of

88
00:06:20.175 --> 00:06:20.575
the house.

89
00:06:21.475 --> 00:06:24.636
Looking out, Meg burst out laughing at the comical sight.

90
00:06:26.268 --> 00:06:32.553
An old horse was pulling an older wagon with great effort while the passengers, her sisters, waved enthusiastically

91
00:06:32.593 --> 00:06:33.173
from the cart.

92
00:06:33.193 --> 00:06:35.255
"Delivery for Mrs.

93
00:06:35.315 --> 00:06:36.155
Meg Brookes!"

94
00:06:36.475 --> 00:06:41.139
Jo shouted as she jumped out and, grabbing a few baskets, headed toward Meg's open door.

95
00:06:42.199 --> 00:06:47.163
Amy and Beth followed suit and soon, after several trips, because there was a lot to carry in,

96
00:06:48.104 --> 00:06:52.367
Meg's kitchen and dining room table were filled with the lavish food prepared for Amy's party.

97
00:06:52.387 --> 00:06:53.808
"Oh, girls!

98
00:06:54.396 --> 00:06:55.457
I don't know what to say!"

99
00:06:55.757 --> 00:06:57.438
Meg cried, her eyes shining brightly.

100
00:06:57.458 --> 00:07:01.480
"We can't possibly eat all this food ourselves," said Amy.

101
00:07:01.500 --> 00:07:05.442
"It looks like a feast fit for a king," Meg praised.

102
00:07:06.022 --> 00:07:07.483
"John will be so pleased."

103
00:07:08.343 --> 00:07:10.104
"We make a good team, don't you think?"

104
00:07:10.424 --> 00:07:10.885
asked Jo.

105
00:07:10.905 --> 00:07:13.066
"We sure do," said Amy.

106
00:07:13.086 --> 00:07:17.088
"Through thick and thin, we March girls know how to stick together."
